This appears to be a **highly multi-modal and rugged function**.

The initial large and highly variable lengthscales suggest a complex global landscape, while the later convergence to consistently small lengthscales indicates a very "rugged" or high-frequency local behavior once a promising region was identified. The frequent need to employ exploration-focused acquisition functions (UCB, TS, qPES, qMES) and the recurrent drops in "shortest distance" followed by increases after exploration steps further support the presence of numerous local minima, characteristic of such functions.
